Falsifies `extensible_host_controller_interface::verification::a_slot_context_keeps_each_field_in_its_own_bits`.

The defect: `slot` forgets to mask the speed id to its four bits, so a speed id above 15 spills into the context count and the reserved bits beside it.

Expected to fail: the harness's check that dword 0 holds nothing outside the speed and context count fields, or that the speed reads back masked to four bits.

diff --git a/src/context.rs b/src/context.rs
--- a/src/context.rs
+++ b/src/context.rs
@@ -49,7 +49,7 @@
 /// context is DCI `entries`. Route string 0: the device is on a root port, not behind a hub.
 pub const fn slot(speed: u8, port: u8, entries: u8) -> [u32; 8] {
     [
-        (speed as u32 & 0xf) << 20 | (entries as u32 & 0x1f) << 27,
+        (speed as u32) << 20 | (entries as u32 & 0x1f) << 27,
         (port as u32) << 16,
         0,
         0,
